      "id": 8,
      "options": {
        "content": "## Grafana is the query layer, not the backend\n\nEvery panel here asks **Prometheus**. No metric is stored in Grafana.\n\n- Hit **/orders** in the demo app to create orders.\n- Traces are not stored here either: open **Explore → Jaeger** in the left sidebar. It is the same Jaeger you see at [localhost:16686](http://localhost:16686).\n- **Reset the demo** on `/orders` deletes the `demo_*` series; these panels go flat until you create new orders.\n- Datasources: Prometheus `http://prometheus:9090`, Jaeger `http://jaeger:16686`.\n\nIf you want Grafana to *receive* OTLP instead of reading another backend, that is a different product: **Tempo** for traces, **Loki** for logs, **Mimir** for metrics — or Grafana Cloud. See the README.\n- HTTP and queue panels come from the same `/metrics` scrape: requests and latency by route, queue depth, failed jobs, and the age of the oldest waiting job.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "How this fits",
      "type": "text"
    },
